bin/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Anchored to the repo root so this ignores only a stray binary built there
# (e.g. `go build` with no -o); without the leading slash the bare name would
# also match the cmd/tierd SOURCE dir, silently dropping any new file added
# under it. Built binaries normally land in bin/ (ignored above).
/tierd
# Local Claude Code / agent workspace state.
#
# Scoped deliberately rather than a blanket `.claude/`: tool configuration that
# a contributor would want on a fresh clone is tracked; only genuinely
# machine-local state (per-machine settings, worktrees, vendored modules) is
# ignored here.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/**/node_modules/

# The Model Report instrument is its own repo (tiermetric/model-bench).
# Never vendor it into tier — an errant `git add -A` can do exactly that.
model-bench/

# >>> tool-managed: agent durability >>>
.claude/agents/*.md
.claude/agent-memory-local/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
# <<< tool-managed: agent durability <<<

# Re-include these files, overriding the tool-managed block above: the manifest
# that block relies on records only metadata, so without this the contents are
# not reproducible from the repo alone.
!.claude/agents/*.md

# Compiled docgen artifact. The Makefile only ever runs `go run .`, so this is
# always a stray `go build` -- and it is a binary embedding local build paths,
# which should never be committed or published.
tools/docgen/docgen
